<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but there are some general outliers that come ahead due to raw stat difference, utility, or an on-use ability.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Assassination Rogues</h4>Engineering remains the same powerhouse it has always been and continues to be the 1 primary profession you will have to be the most optimal you can be. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is the main reason for this with its Mists of Pandaria version granting us 1920 primary stat for 10 seconds on a 1 minute cooldown. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142568/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_burningspeed.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> continues to function the same way offering a big speed boost for 5 seconds and attached to your belt socket. There are no new explosives in Mists of Pandaria, so the profession does take a light hit in that regard.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Assassination Rogues</h4>Tailoring offers <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> with its new version giving 4000 attack power for 15 seconds on a ~1 minute internal cooldown. If you're able to effectively track the proc and line it up with other cooldowns, this profession should at least be tied for 2nd best.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Assassination Rogues</h4>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=164/blacksmithing">
<img alt="Blacksmithing" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_blacksmithing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blacksmithing</span></a> offers the same raw agility bonus as the other professions. What sets it apart from the other standard 320 Agility professions is the ability to stack a large amount of secondary stats which Assassination may end up favoring due to its high value on Haste.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="herbalism">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_herbalism.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Herbalism for Subtlety Rogues</h4>Didn't expect to see this profession rear its head in Phase 3, did ya? The burst of haste <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=121279/lifeblood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_wispsplodegreen.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifeblood</span></a> granted is massive during burst windows and starts to be a major contender with the other professions.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Best Crafted Gear for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h3>Crafted items are a great way to get an early boost to your item level and bolster up your stats. While some do require you to be leveled up in the profession that crafts them, there are several BoE options as well that can be bought and sold.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77534/agile-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Agile Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Retinal Armor</span></a> as per every other expansion, remains the best option that we have prior to raiding. This is crafted with the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
